---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Source from '../components/Source.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
import { links, iso, biosMenu, uefiMenu } from '../data/site';

const isoFile = 'katlinux-YYYY.MM.DD-x86_64.iso';
---

<Base
  title="Download"
  description="Download the Kat Linux live ISO, learn how the file is named, and write it to a USB stick with Ventoy, balenaEtcher or dd."
>
  <PageHead eyebrow="Download" title="Get the live ISO">
    One ISO for BIOS and UEFI PCs. It boots into a live Xfce desktop with archinstall ready when you are.
  </PageHead>

  <section class="section dl">
    <div class="wrap dl__grid">
      <div class="dl__main">
        <Callout tone="warning" title="Kat Linux is in early development">
          <p>
            Only the base ISO is ticked off in the project's to-do list, and every push to the repository produces a
            new build. Try it in a virtual machine or on a spare computer first, and don't trust it with anything
            important yet.
          </p>
        </Callout>

        <div class="panel eared">
          <div class="panel__head">
            <p class="eyebrow">Latest build</p>
            <h2>Kat Linux live ISO</h2>
            <p class="panel__file mono">{isoFile}</p>
          </div>
          <a class="btn btn-primary btn-big panel__btn" href={links.release}>
            <Icon name="download" />
            Download from GitHub
          </a>
          <p class="panel__note">
            The ISO is attached to the <a href={links.release}>“latest” release</a> on GitHub. If you see more than
            one ISO there, take the one with the newest date in its name.
          </p>
          <dl class="facts">
            <div><dt>Architecture</dt><dd>{iso.arch} (64-bit PCs)</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Firmware</dt><dd>BIOS and UEFI</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Live user</dt><dd><code>archie</code>, logged in automatically</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Built by</dt><dd>GitHub Actions, on every push to <code>main</code></dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="dl__aside">
        <h2 class="aside-title">Before you flash</h2>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>A USB stick you can erase. Its contents will be lost.</li>
          <li>A 64-bit (x86_64) PC, or a virtual machine.</li>
          <li>A wired connection is easiest. Wi-Fi works from the terminal with <code>iwctl</code>.</li>
          <li>
            Secure Boot turned off. The profile doesn't set up Secure Boot signing, so firmware that enforces it may
            refuse to start the stick.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="aside-more">
          Next: <a href={href('/install/')}>the install guide <Icon name="arrow" size={16} /></a>
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="naming-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">File name</p>
        <h2 id="naming-title">How the ISO is named</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          The name is put together by <code>mkarchiso</code> from the values in <code>profiledef.sh</code>, so you can
          tell from the file name alone which build you have.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="anatomy" aria-label="Anatomy of the ISO file name">
        <p class="anatomy__name mono" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="seg seg--a">katlinux</span><span class="sep">-</span><span class="seg seg--b">2026.11.07</span><span class="sep">-</span><span class="seg seg--c">x86_64</span><span class="sep">.iso</span>
        </p>
        <dl class="anatomy__parts">
          <div class="part part--a">
            <dt><code>katlinux</code></dt>
            <dd>The <code>iso_name</code>. Every Kat Linux ISO starts with it.</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="part part--b">
            <dt><code>YYYY.MM.DD</code></dt>
            <dd>
              The <code>iso_version</code>: the date the ISO was built. The example shows what a build from 7 November
              2026 would be called.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div class="part part--c">
            <dt><code>x86_64</code></dt>
            <dd>The CPU architecture. It is the only one Kat Linux builds for.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <figcaption>
          <span>
            When written to a USB stick, the volume label is <code>{iso.label}</code>, for example
            <code>KAT_202611</code>.
          </span>
          <Source path="profiledef.sh" />
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <Callout title="No checksums yet" class="naming-note">
        <p>
          The build workflow uploads only the ISO, with no checksum or signature files next to it. Verifying downloads
          is a good first contribution if you want one.
        </p>
        <p><Source path=".github/workflows/buildiso.yml" /></p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="flash-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Write it to USB</p>
        <h2 id="flash-title">Flash the ISO</h2>
        <p class="muted">Pick one of the three tools below. They all give you a bootable stick.</p>
      </div>

      <Callout tone="danger" title="This wipes the drive">
        <p>
          balenaEtcher and <code>dd</code> overwrite the whole USB stick. Installing Ventoy also erases the stick, the
          first time only. Copy anything you want to keep off it first, and double-check you picked the right drive:
          <code>dd</code> will happily overwrite your system disk if you tell it to.
        </p>
      </Callout>

      <nav class="tool-nav" aria-label="Flashing tools">
        <a href="#ventoy"><strong>Ventoy</strong><span>Keep several ISOs on one stick</span></a>
        <a href="#etcher"><strong>balenaEtcher</strong><span>Point and click, on Windows, macOS and Linux</span></a>
        <a href="#dd"><strong>dd</strong><span>One command, on any Linux system</span></a>
      </nav>

      <div class="tools">
        <article class="tool" id="ventoy" aria-labelledby="ventoy-title">
          <header>
            <h3 id="ventoy-title">Ventoy</h3>
            <a class="ext" href={links.ventoy}>ventoy.net <Icon name="external" size={14} /></a>
          </header>
          <ol class="mini-steps">
            <li>Install Ventoy onto the USB stick with Ventoy2Disk. This erases the stick once.</li>
            <li>Copy the <code>katlinux-…-x86_64.iso</code> file onto the stick like any other file.</li>
            <li>Boot from the stick and choose the Kat Linux ISO from Ventoy's list.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="tool__note">Later builds can sit next to the old one. Just copy the new file over.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="tool" id="etcher" aria-labelledby="etcher-title">
          <header>
            <h3 id="etcher-title">balenaEtcher</h3>
            <a class="ext" href={links.etcher}>etcher.balena.io <Icon name="external" size={14} /></a>
          </header>
          <ol class="mini-steps">
            <li>Open balenaEtcher and choose <strong>Flash from file</strong>, then pick the ISO.</li>
            <li>Choose <strong>Select target</strong> and pick your USB stick.</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Flash!</strong> and wait for it to finish validating.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="tool__note">Etcher checks the written data afterwards, which catches bad sticks.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="tool tool--wide" id="dd" aria-labelledby="dd-title">
          <header>
            <h3 id="dd-title"><code>dd</code> on Linux</h3>
          </header>
          <ol class="mini-steps">
            <li>
              <p>Plug in the stick and find its device name. Go by the size and model, not the order.</p>
              <CodeBlock label="Find the USB stick" code="lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,TRAN" />
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>If your desktop mounted it, unmount its partitions.</p>
              <CodeBlock label="Unmount" code="sudo umount /dev/sdX?*" />
            </li>
            <li>
              <p>
                Write the ISO. Replace <code>/dev/sdX</code> with the whole device (like <code>/dev/sdb</code>), not
                a partition (like <code>/dev/sdb1</code>), and use your real file name.
              </p>
              <CodeBlock
                label="Write the ISO (erases the stick)"
                code="sudo dd if=katlinux-YYYY.MM.DD-x86_64.iso of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress oflag=sync"
              />
            </li>
          </ol>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="firmware-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Booting</p>
        <h2 id="firmware-title">UEFI and BIOS</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          The ISO carries a boot menu for each firmware type. Start the PC with the stick plugged in and open its
          one-time boot menu (often <kbd>F12</kbd>, <kbd>F11</kbd>, <kbd>F8</kbd> or <kbd>Esc</kbd>, depending on
          the maker).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Boot menus on the Kat Linux ISO">
        <table>
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Boot menus on the Kat Linux ISO</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Firmware</th>
              <th scope="col">Boot menu</th>
              <th scope="col">Entries</th>
              <th scope="col">Auto-boot</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">BIOS / legacy</th>
              <td>syslinux, titled “Kat Linux”, over the boot splash</td>
              <td>
                <ul class="cell-list">
                  {biosMenu.entries.map((e) => <li>{e.label}</li>)}
                </ul>
              </td>
              <td class="mono">{biosMenu.timeoutSeconds} s</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">UEFI</th>
              <td>systemd-boot</td>
              <td>
                <ul class="cell-list">
                  {uefiMenu.entries.map((e) => <li>{e}</li>)}
                </ul>
              </td>
              <td class="mono">{uefiMenu.timeoutSeconds} s</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="table-source">
        <Source path={['profiledef.sh', 'syslinux/', 'efiboot/loader/']} />
      </p>

      <div class="notes">
        <div>
          <h3>The UEFI menu still says “Arch Linux”</h3>
          <p>
            The systemd-boot entries haven't been renamed yet. It is the same Kat Linux ISO either way; pick the first
            entry.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Screen reader</h3>
          <p>
            Both menus have an entry with speech, which starts the speakup screen reader. On the BIOS menu, press
            <kbd>S</kbd> to jump to it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Virtual machines</h3>
          <p>
            Guest tools for QEMU, VirtualBox, VMware and Hyper-V are on the ISO, so it is comfortable to test in a VM
            before touching real hardware.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .dl__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 3vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .dl__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .dl__main {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* ---- the eared download panel ---- */
  .panel {
    --ear-color: var(--ink);
    --ear-inset: 10%;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 2vw, 2.25rem);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--card);
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
  }

  .panel__head {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .panel h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }

  .panel__file {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .panel__btn {
    justify-self: start;
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .panel__btn {
      justify-self: stretch;
    }
  }

  .panel__note {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }

  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 12rem), 1fr));
    gap: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .facts div {
    padding: 0.8rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .facts dt {
    font-family: var(--type-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ---- aside ---- */
  .dl__aside {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-content: start;
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .aside-title {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .checklist li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.85rem 0 0.85rem 1.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .checklist li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.15rem;
    top: 1.15rem;
    width: 0.95rem;
    height: 0.95rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--nose);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .aside-more a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* ---- anatomy of the file name ---- */
  .anatomy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 2vw, 2.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--card);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .anatomy__name {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 0.5rem + 3.2vw, 2.6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .seg {
    border-bottom: 4px solid currentColor;
    padding-bottom: 0.05em;
  }

  .seg--a,
  .part--a dt code {
    color: var(--nose);
  }

  .seg--b,
  .part--b dt code {
    color: var(--iris);
  }

  .seg--c,
  .part--c dt code {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sep {
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .anatomy__parts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem 2rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 14rem), 1fr));
  }

  .part {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    align-content: start;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 3px solid currentColor;
  }

  .part--a {
    color: var(--nose);
  }

  .part--b {
    color: var(--iris);
  }

  .part--c {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .part dt code {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }

  .part dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .anatomy figcaption {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  :global(.naming-note) {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  /* ---- flashing tools ---- */
  .tool-nav {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 14rem), 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .tool-nav a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .tool-nav a:hover {
    border-color: var(--nose);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .tool-nav strong {
    font-family: var(--type-display);
    font-stretch: 110%;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .tool-nav span {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .tools {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .tools {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .tool--wide {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }

  .tool {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-content: start;
    padding: clamp(1.1rem, 1rem + 1vw, 1.75rem);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--card);
    border-radius: 0 0 var(--radius-m) var(--radius-m);
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .tool header {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
  }

  .tool h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .tool h3 code {
    font-size: 0.95em;
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .ext {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .mini-steps {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  .mini-steps li {
    padding-left: 0.25rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .mini-steps li > * + * {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  .mini-steps li::marker {
    font-family: var(--type-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--nose);
  }

  .tool__note {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  /* ---- firmware table ---- */
  .cell-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    font-family: var(--type-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
  }

  td.mono {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  tbody th {
    font-family: var(--type-body);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
    background: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .table-source {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  .notes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 16rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .notes > div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    align-content: start;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .notes p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
</style>
